                    {
                        "form_id": "74d7a916-8f3c-464a-b544-b6fc6c8b4c13",
                        "entry_id": "0cfca487-5e5c-37cc-82c0-b69fe0c9e2ea",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most bigly"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1797e975-6c70-342c-a736-3c6bfdde1205",
                        "entry_id": "0cfca487-5e5c-37cc-82c0-b69fe0c9e2ea",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Habitable, liveable; hence delightful, pleasant, pleasing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2e4c4ed-86c0-4317-9be7-a8988ab9b244",
                                "sense_id": "1797e975-6c70-342c-a736-3c6bfdde1205",
                                "text": "\"And steek it weel, thy biglie bower, / And by the rood thee sain; / And tell thy bedes in haly guise, / Till this ae night is gane!\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "931a39c9-218d-4151-bb57-ac865863bef4",
                                "sense_id": "1797e975-6c70-342c-a736-3c6bfdde1205",
                                "text": "When I was in my bigly bower, / I wore but what I would; / This night I'm lighter 'mang Willie's horse feet, / I fear I'll die for cold."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "63c059d0-9b89-3e66-9146-b9791258c606",
                "word": "bigly",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8d9e7626-168d-4f16-a585-7c01adec81a5",
                        "entry_id": "63c059d0-9b89-3e66-9146-b9791258c606",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more bigly"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e32f55b3-b982-445e-86eb-efdbe5594d60",
                        "entry_id": "63c059d0-9b89-3e66-9146-b9791258c606",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most bigly"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "825b8483-cb26-38a2-816e-7397df4121c5",
                        "entry_id": "63c059d0-9b89-3e66-9146-b9791258c606",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a big way, greatly; to a great extent, on a large scale."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d23595f-7245-4739-9212-469f3d0153ba",
                                "sense_id": "825b8483-cb26-38a2-816e-7397df4121c5",
                                "text": "He looked at Mrs. Harling, who loomed bigly in the dull light."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "60535f89-af4d-413a-93a7-276f753a52f7",
                                "sense_id": "825b8483-cb26-38a2-816e-7397df4121c5",
                                "text": "Big Bessie's feet hurt like nobody's business, / but she stands—bigly—under the unruly scrutiny, stands in the wild weed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e949836e-dc19-4c45-80ec-4e03b7e2034e",
                                "sense_id": "825b8483-cb26-38a2-816e-7397df4121c5",
                                "text": "I have only one real (and ridiculous) reason—the reflection of my awestruck 5 year old face in a head mirror. […] I gripped my mother's hand while she spoke to a big voice from a big face from a big man in a big white coat. He suddenly stopped and turned his big eyes on me. I dug my nails into my mother's hand. He reached out his big hand over the menacing silver array on his desk. I closed my eyes tightly. He said something … bigly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5cdcbf29-4e21-42db-a06d-ab02ba08ba5c",
                                "sense_id": "825b8483-cb26-38a2-816e-7397df4121c5",
                                "text": "I will bigly, hugely admit that I was wrong"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f22a1dd9-36fd-4f22-a284-d153e8e20557",
                                "sense_id": "825b8483-cb26-38a2-816e-7397df4121c5",
                                "text": "In the light and air the shadows of the clouds move bigly over the baby's arms."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e735e5e-e7a1-4e4d-a52b-8281f1650d49",
                                "sense_id": "825b8483-cb26-38a2-816e-7397df4121c5",
                                "text": "By the way, isn't my handwriting more appropriate now? You complained that I was writing too bigly for airletters and sort of cheating you of information."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4a1ffe4-bf26-4bb2-b737-ebcca0d39532",
                                "sense_id": "825b8483-cb26-38a2-816e-7397df4121c5",
                                "text": "Halfway through the song, the audience decided that they actually really loved me because they started clapping and whooping and standing up. I smiled really bigly' and sang louder."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b15d008-443f-4e22-a2f9-1698ae544cad",
                                "sense_id": "825b8483-cb26-38a2-816e-7397df4121c5",
                                "text": "That is, start to renegotiate, gain some minor concessions then declare victory bigly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c2004f7-dfb1-4254-be49-7dc1c464452b",
                                "sense_id": "825b8483-cb26-38a2-816e-7397df4121c5",
                                "text": "What was the strange urgency? The thought hovered bigly […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "59faea09-3a95-4191-a7cf-62e5aca1f59c",
                                "sense_id": "825b8483-cb26-38a2-816e-7397df4121c5",
                                "text": "Klobuchar delivered in Biden's moment of need. Bigly, as some might say. Her gift should be just as bigly."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3ba1abc4-cce3-390f-9b05-30bb09bb64f2",
                        "entry_id": "63c059d0-9b89-3e66-9146-b9791258c606",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Strongly, with great force."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3abec8e9-7208-45e0-a72c-0b5b97c06da6",
                                "sense_id": "3ba1abc4-cce3-390f-9b05-30bb09bb64f2",
                                "text": "Thesse men did much in order to publicke good, befor they spake biglie; bot done nothing since, saue that they haue drawin away considerable forces, raissed at wast charges for the publicke defence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "99eedde8-43c6-4a28-9e1d-215812a578da",
                                "sense_id": "3ba1abc4-cce3-390f-9b05-30bb09bb64f2",
                                "text": "It was well obſerved by the late pious Dr Doddridge, that \"The eternal ſalvation of one ſoul is of far greater importance, and bigly pregnant with far greater events, than the temporal ſalvation, wealth, well-being, or happiness of a whole kingdom, though it were for the ſpace of ten thouſand, or of ten millions of ages;[…]\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e38c7b4a-76a0-4ea5-a6a8-d1ec71a05c51",
                                "sense_id": "3ba1abc4-cce3-390f-9b05-30bb09bb64f2",
                                "text": "Tell me about The Mamas & Papas^([sic]), Bob. I believe you’re backing them very bigly, and they’re great. I believe you're backing them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b3cb0fd-d8b2-4f75-99bd-ff4739bb7007",
                                "sense_id": "3ba1abc4-cce3-390f-9b05-30bb09bb64f2",
                                "text": "And he [Henry David Thoreau] was very strong to, for the, for the—against slavery. He was very bigly against that. Slavery was going on in America, enslaving the black people."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3a431eac-516a-3db2-833f-523b3161febb",
                        "entry_id": "63c059d0-9b89-3e66-9146-b9791258c606",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a blustering or boastful manner; haughtily, pompously."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "add9272b-3d9a-4fc9-b23f-e3079f3eeb94",
                                "sense_id": "3a431eac-516a-3db2-833f-523b3161febb",
                                "text": "Would'ſt thou not rather chooſe a ſmall renown, / To be the mayor of ſome poor paltry town, / Bigly to look, and barbarouſly to ſpeak; / To pound falſe weights, and ſcanty meaſures break?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c8bf73f-e608-4fae-ab15-df0c76c742c5",
                                "sense_id": "3a431eac-516a-3db2-833f-523b3161febb",
                                "text": "In any event, he adopted the whole of [William] Lauder's malignity; and let his partisans first clear him of this offense before they talk bigly of his innocence, and bluster in his cause."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "46112242-f7ff-454d-8557-bb4caa31ab3c",
                                "sense_id": "3a431eac-516a-3db2-833f-523b3161febb",
                                "text": "Of the Three General Modes of Newspaper Amplification, the first is adapted to persons who talk bigly without difficulty. Its Effect is indeed admirable. There is no fact or conceit so trivial and foolish that it may not be metamorphosed into the Highest Wisdom, or, at least, into the Tone and Semblance of the Highest Wisdom, by the Polysyllabic Method of Spreading. But to those who find it difficult to talk bigly, the adaptation of this method will be attended with the labour of a frequent recurrence to the Dictionary, a thing to be sedulously avoided by all who desire to novel politely, that is to say, easily, alike to Reader and to Writer."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
